# Katherine's Portfolio — Cursor Rules

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS (dark mode via `class` strategy)
- Framer Motion for all animations
- Lenis for smooth scroll

## Design Tokens — always use these, never hardcode hex values

### Surfaces (dark mode first, always)
- Page bg: `bg-surface-950` (#09090b)
- Sidebar: `bg-surface-900` (#18181b)
- Cards: `bg-surface-800` (#27272a)
- Borders: `border-surface-700` (#3f3f46)

### Text
- Primary: `text-zinc-100`
- Secondary: `text-zinc-400`
- Muted: `text-zinc-500`
- Dimmer: `text-zinc-600`

### Accent
- Main: `text-accent` / `bg-accent` (violet-400, #a78bfa)
- Dim: `bg-accent-dim` (violet-600)
- Muted bg: `bg-accent-muted` (violet-950)

## Component conventions
- All components are in `src/components/`
- Layout components: `src/components/layout/`
- UI atoms: `src/components/ui/`
- All data lives in `src/lib/data.ts` — never hardcode content in components
- Use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts` for conditional class merging

## Animation principles
- Entry animations: fade + translateY(12–20px), duration 0.4–0.5s, ease [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]
- Stagger siblings: 0.06–0.08s delay increments
- Hover: subtle y: -4, duration 0.2s ease-out
- Never use CSS transitions for complex animations — always Framer Motion
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` via Framer Motion's `useReducedMotion()`

## File structure
src/
  app/
    layout.tsx          ← root layout with Sidebar + SmoothScroll
    page.tsx            ← home / work index
    about/page.tsx      ← about page
    work/[slug]/page.tsx ← case study template
  components/
    layout/
      Sidebar.tsx
      SmoothScroll.tsx
    ui/
      ProjectCard.tsx
  lib/
    data.ts             ← ALL content lives here
    utils.ts            ← cn() helper
  styles/
    globals.css

## Cursor prompting tips
- "Add a [component] using existing tokens from tailwind.config.ts"
- "Animate this with Framer Motion, stagger children by 0.07s"
- "Keep it dark mode — no hardcoded colors"
- "Add micro-interaction: [describe what should happen on hover/click]"
